e general, a figure who epitomized the radical Taborite resistance in the aftermath of the Hussite Wars. Descending from the Bohemian gentry, Roháč became a symbol of unwavering commitment to the Hussite cause, even as the movement fractured and its main forces were defeated. His tenacious holdout against the combined might of Imperial and moderate Hussite forces solidified his place as a tragic hero and a final, uncompromised voice of the Hussite revolution, influencing both popular memory and subsequent national narratives in Bohemia.

